			<div class="content" id="post-content-4846860">
									

<p>Hm. I'm going to make a really radical suggestion here: this should be a tale. This feels like you're really trying to tell this deeply personal, highly emotional tale of what happens to a Foundation researcher assigned to work with this, and the effect it has on their mental health; and I think that could really work, particularly considering how easily this SCP can escape. But not as a SCP: where the therapy details and the intimate personal feelings of the researcher would feel extremely out of place. Instead, doing this as a tale, likely from the perspective of the researcher but possibly from the perspective of they're therapist or something, would really allow you to convey the emotional turmoil a lot better.</p>
<p>Equally, you're welcome to see if a different reviewer would appreciate this more: it's very possible the idea just doesn't sit right with me personally rather than it being flawed.</p>

							</div>

								
					
