<p>With the changes you've made, it kinda feels like this has a big thematic/narrative disconnect in it: like, it still opens on dealing with the violent authoritarianism of the Brazilian government, but this is very quickly put aside for a story very focussed on the Foundation kinda playing around with it; and it feels&#8230;like the first stuff is a lot more unique and a lot stronger narratively and this just, really needs that to be explored more rather than introducing this big b plot about like, earthquakes and termination and an MTF getting eaten; or at least for that stuff to be tied directly into the actions of the government earlier?</p>
<p>Idk, I feel like you've certainly improved the narrative elements in this a lot but it's in a direction I personally don't really vibe with.</p>

